    "created_at": "2017-10-11T01:15:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-11T01:15:40Z",
    "body": "Also note that making dedicated workers always inherit the service worker would reduce the planned utility of the registration scope.  In theory the plan was to allow workers to be controlled by a separate service worker from the owner document.  Or for only one to be controlled and not the other.  Clearly sites have reported overhead from FetchEvent, so I'm not sure we should throw out the capability to separate ServiceWorkers here casually.\r\n\r\nAlso, for my edification, what is the use case driving this change?  Is it just the desire to have cross-origin top level worker scripts?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
